{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPositivityPredicate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobeniusPositivityPredicate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.entriesNonneg_gram_of_symm_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.entriesNonneg_gram_of_symm_idem","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L279-L290","doc":"The Gram matrix of a family of symmetric idempotents is entrywise\nnonnegative -- exactly the hypothesis `frobPos_of_entriesNonneg` needs.\n\nSo for such a family Frobenius positivity is implied by coordinatewise\npositivity, and therefore excludes nothing from the nonnegative orthant: the\nconstraint is **loose**. This is the general statement behind the corpus's own\nreport of `N_ℓ = 84` feasible ILP solutions for the proton -- a count that is\nlarge precisely because the constraint is weak. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.trace_mul_nonneg_of_symm_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.trace_mul_nonneg_of_symm_idem","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L252-L277","doc":"**The structural fact.** For *symmetric idempotent* matrices `P` and `Q`,\n`tr(P Q) ≥ 0`.\n\nThe proof is the identity `tr(P Q) = tr((P Q)ᵀ (P Q))`, which holds because\n`(PQ)ᵀ (PQ) = Q P P Q = Q P Q` and `tr(Q P Q) = tr(P Q²) = tr(P Q)` by\ncyclicity and idempotency. The right-hand side is a sum of squares.\n\nThis is what makes the Frobenius Gram matrix of a family of idempotents\nentrywise nonnegative, block by block, and hence -- once weighted by\nnonnegative `y_λ` -- what makes `EntriesNonneg` hold for the `G` the corpus\ndefines. The nonnegativity measured at `k = 3` and across the `k ≤ 2`\nfiltration is this identity, not a numerical accident. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.trace_transpose_mul_self_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.trace_transpose_mul_self_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L243-L250","doc":"`tr(Aᵀ A) ≥ 0`: the trace of `Aᵀ A` is the sum of the squares of the\nentries of `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.stableAt_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.stableAt_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L203-L211","doc":"The relaxed stability predicate is trivially satisfied, for every `G`.\n\nThis is a *sharpness* result, not a useful one: it shows the corpus's condition\ncarries content only through the constraint this relaxation drops -- that `x`\nbe the primitive-basis decomposition of the given normal form `T_w`, with\nnonnegative **integer** coordinates. Any formalisation aiming to decide\nstability for a nucleon must carry that constraint, or it proves nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.StableAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.StableAt","kind":"def","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L193-L200","doc":"**Stability**, as `def:stable-atom` defines it: some nonnegative selection\nvector is Frobenius-positive.\n\nStated over an ordered ring; the corpus's integrality (`x ∈ ℤ_{≥0}^N`) is the\nstrictly stronger ILP condition, and `stable-atom-properties.md` is explicit\nthat the two differ (\"the ILP version is strictly stronger\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.naive_reading_unsound_of_neg_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.naive_reading_unsound_of_neg_entry","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L183-L191","doc":"Restated as the contrapositive an agent should actually check: if the Gram\nmatrix has any negative entry, the naive reading is unsound and its verdicts\ncarry no information about stability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.coordPos_imp_frobPos_iff_entriesNonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.coordPos_imp_frobPos_iff_entriesNonneg","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L164-L181","doc":"**The characterisation.** Over a nontrivial index set, the naive reading is\nsound for *every* selection vector exactly when the Gram matrix is entrywise\nnonnegative.\n\nSo substituting coordinatewise positivity for Frobenius positivity is not a\nharmless simplification that happens to fail on adversarial input: it is\nlicensed only by a hypothesis on `G` that a Frobenius Gram matrix has no reason\nto satisfy, and that must be checked before the substitution is made. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.exists_coordPos_not_frobPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.exists_coordPos_not_frobPos","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L140-L162","doc":"**The separation.** A single negative Gram entry `G γ₀ i₀ < 0` already\nexhibits a coordinatewise-positive vector that is *not* Frobenius-positive:\nthe indicator of `i₀`.\n\nThis is the failure mode the docstring describes, as a theorem. The witness is\nthe simplest vector there is, so the two predicates are not merely inequivalent\nin the abstract -- they part company on the basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_of_entriesNonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_of_entriesNonneg","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L133-L138","doc":"If the Gram matrix is entrywise nonnegative then the naive reading is\n*sound*: coordinatewise positivity of `x` does imply Frobenius positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_smul","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L119-L127","doc":"Frobenius positivity is closed under nonnegative scaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_add","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L108-L117","doc":"Frobenius positivity is closed under addition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobPos_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L99-L106","doc":"The zero selection is always Frobenius-positive, so the *relaxed* feasible\nset is never empty. This is the formal content of the parenthetical in\n`stable-atom-properties.md`, \"the continuous LP relaxation is always feasible\":\nemptiness is never the obstruction, integrality and the decomposition\nconstraint are. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.EntriesNonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.EntriesNonneg","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L93-L94","doc":"Entrywise nonnegativity of the Gram matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CoordPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CoordPos","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**The naive reading**: every coordinate of the vector is itself `≥ 0`.\n\nDefinitionally `SelectionNonneg`; named separately because the two play\ndifferent roles -- this is what an agent substitutes *for* `FrobPos`, whereas\n`SelectionNonneg` is a genuine part of the corpus's condition alongside it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.SelectionNonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.SelectionNonneg","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L82-L84","doc":"The selection vector is nonnegative -- the `x ∈ ℤ_{≥0}^N` half of the\ncorpus's condition, relaxed to an ordered ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobPos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.FrobPos","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/FrobeniusPositivityPredicate.lean#L74-L80","doc":"**Frobenius positivity**, verbatim from `def:stable-atom`: the constraint\n`(G x)_γ ≥ 0` holds for every primitive constraint `γ`.\n\n`x` is the coordinate vector in the primitive Wedderburn basis `{e_λ}`; `G` is\nthe Frobenius Gram matrix of those operators. ","signatureChunk":0}]}